  "body": "Whilst investigating #1748, i saw even weirder behaviour in @vberger's logs.  As well as having accumulated a bunch of graph extremities for #rust (see #1760), something was causing synapse to try to do resolution on current room state for #rust on pretty much every request (both CS and SS!)... as well as hundreds which weren't even associated with a request context.\r\n\r\nfor instance, an innocent 'set present' CS request would take 30s, with 20s of CPU time, thanks to the merge:\r\n\r\n```\r\n2017-01-04 15:23:35,238 - synapse.access.http.8008 - 59 - INFO - PUT-273116 - 213.137.178.134 - 8008 - Received request: PUT /_matrix/client/r0/presence/%40levans%3Asafaradeg.net/status?access_token=<redacted>\r\n2017-01-04 15:23:35,272 - synapse.storage._base - 242 - WARNING - PUT-273116 - [TXN OPERROR] {update_presence-fa365} could not serialize access due to concurrent update\r\n2017-01-04 15:23:35,754 - synapse.state - 310 - INFO - PUT-273116 - Resolving state for !PcCidzjUKXHKImhTrB:matrix.org with 21 groups\r\n2017-01-04 15:23:35,945 - synapse.state - 325 - INFO - PUT-273116 - Resolving conflicted state for '!PcCidzjUKXHKImhTrB:matrix.org'\r\n2017-01-04 15:24:04,359 - synapse.access.http.8008 - 91 - INFO - PUT-273116 - 213.137.178.134 - 8008 - {@levans:safaradeg.net} Processed request: 29121ms (19259ms, 60ms) (53ms/1) 22B 200 \"PUT /_matrix/client/r0/presence/%40levans%3Asafaradeg.net/status?access_token=<redacted> HTTP/1.0\" \"Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:50.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/50.0\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n...similarly /sync requests, and /typing, etc.  wtf?",
